  "pre_registered_primary_endpoint": "majority_hit component-macro @1 (the locked selection criterion). The selected arm does NOT clear random on it (p=0.1225). Wins at @5 majority-hit (p=0.0100) and @1 half-epitope (p=0.0050) are SECONDARY endpoints, not pre-specified, among 32 arm x metric x k comparisons.",
  "headline_findings": [
    "The SHIPPED PRINCE site ranker (original_incumbent) is statistically indistinguishable from random patch selection at every k on majority-hit (z = +0.0/+0.1/-0.5/-0.3). Its advertised 69/110 top-10 majority-hit equals the random-control rate.",
    "Exposure-alone is WORSE than random at top-5 and top-10 (z = -1.8, -2.3): ranking by maximum solvent exposure actively steers proposals away from antibody epitopes.",
    "The new patch-level XGBoost learning-to-rank model is the first PRINCE arm to exceed the random control, but only at secondary endpoints.",
    "It does NOT beat the shipped model head-to-head (all paired CIs include zero) and is worse on raw unweighted counts. Its gains are concentrated in small antigen clusters."
